Search Complexity
•	Linked List Search: O(n)
•	Python List Search: O(n)
Although both are O(n), Python lists are much faster in practice because elements are stored in contiguous memory locations.
2. CPU Cache Locality
Python lists store elements next to each other in memory. This improves CPU cache performance because nearby data can be loaded together.
Linked lists store nodes in different memory locations. The CPU must follow pointers from one node to another, causing slower memory access.
3. Memory Overhead
Each linked-list node stores:
•	Ticket data
•	A pointer (next)
This extra pointer increases memory usage.
Python lists only store the elements and therefore use memory more efficiently.



